urce 10.1.1.1', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco configuration for the specified Juniper BGP neighbor commands:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 65410\\n neighbor 10.1.1.2 remote-as 100\\n neighbor 10.1.1.2 update-source 10.1.1.1\\n neighbor 10.1.1.2 route-map direct-import in\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. The Cisco configuration requires the BGP AS to be specified in the `router bgp` command first\\n2. The `remote-as` corresponds to Juniper's `peer-as`\\n3. The `update-source` corresponds to Juniper's `local-address`\\n4. Cisco uses `route-map` instead of `import` for policy application\\n5. You would need to separately configure the `route-map direct-import` to match the Juniper policy-statement behavior\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 10.1.1.2 update-source 10.1.1.1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 10.1.1.2 route-map direct-import in', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco configuration for the specified Juniper BGP neighbor commands:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 65410\\n neighbor 10.1.1.2 remote-as 100\\n neighbor 10.1.1.2 update-source 10.1.1.1\\n neighbor 10.1.1.2 route-map direct-import in\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. The Cisco configuration requires the BGP AS to be specified in the `router bgp` command first\\n2. The `remote-as` corresponds to Juniper's `peer-as`\\n3. The `update-source` corresponds to Juniper's `local-address`\\n4. Cisco uses `route-map` instead of `import` for policy application\\n5. You would need to separately configure the `route-map direct-import` to match the Juniper policy-statement behavior\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 10.1.1.2 route-map direct-import in'}]]": 1,
